  "title": "kits.json: each character's, weapon's and set's kit, generated from Genshin Optimizer's Waverider sheets by tools/go-reference (see its README); do not edit it: change the decision files (tools/go-reference/decided/) and run the tool. Percentage stats are fractions (0.466 is 46.6%). An effect adds min(rate x max(stat - over, 0), cap) to its bucket `to`: `stat` is its `from` stat (read before conversions, `premod`, the panel's; or after them, `final`), `over` is in that stat's own units, `cap` is x base ATK when `cap_from` says so, no `from` adds rate itself; it holds while its gates hold: `pieces`, `from_ascension`, `from_constellation`, `talents` (the moves it reaches), `weapon_types`, `hits` (the rows it reaches) and `while` (the toggle that must be on), and, only on the effects that have them, `times` (a second stat of hers it multiplies by, read as `reads` says: Kokomi's Healing Bonus), `in_talent` (the talent whose rows `hits` names, for a row name two talents share) and `also` (the toggles besides `while` that must be on, for a term that reads two or more of her states). A list `rate` is by refinement for a weapon, and by talent level (index: level - 1) when `row` names the talent row it is. `dmg` is DMG Bonus for every hit, `mult` multiplies the hit's multiplier by 1 + rate. `in_stats`: HoYoLAB's panel already holds it for the weapon, set or character it belongs to; the engine adds it only for a tested weapon or set that is not hers. A hit's kind is in `hits`, the element of a Stellar hit in `elements`, the move of a Normal Attack row (and of a Skill or Burst row the game deals as an attack) in `moves`. `row_gates` (some characters): a row, as the planner's block names it, that is dealt only `from` a constellation or only `below` one (Yanfei's Charged Attack with four Scarlet Seals is Constellation 6's). `derived_rows` (some characters): a row of her Skill or Burst that HoYoLAB prints no row for, named in our own words, with the numbers of `from_row`, a row of `from_talent` (Sethos's Dusk Bolts have his Normal Attack's). `party` (some characters): the team shapes her damage depends on, `default` the usual one (`reason` says why), each option with the elements the rows that take the team's element deal; `element_rows` are those rows (dealt once for each element of the option) and `only_rows` the rows only some options deal; an effect with `party` holds only in those options.",
